<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dis-sēmĭno</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v.
			a.—<b>Lit.</b>, to scatter seed, to
		sow; hence, trop., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to spread abroad</i>, <i>disseminate</i> (rare,
			but good prose); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coupled with spargere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Arch. 12, 30</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Planc. 23, 56</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malum latius opinione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Cat.
					4, 3 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causam morbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					12, 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cupidines populis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rumorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 6 al.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scientiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 15, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
